{"ts":"2026-08-10T20:46:45.822Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"93c1cb9c51cd52f327b34f44","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.226","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-9gzr4r"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The edge-count floor is denominated over a population that includes the edges the graph itself calls redundant, so repairing 73 witnessed implied ordering rows and silently relaxing the guard are the same privileged act"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"pm graph redundancy computes 73 transitively implied ordering edges (35 blocks + 38 blocked_by), each carrying a witness path, so the product already names them as adding no ordering information. graph-profile-edges-floor is denominated in TOTAL deduplicated directed edges and stands at 11871 against 11875 observed, so the gate-admissible repair is at most 4 of 73 (5.5%). Beyond that the run reports floor_undercut, and --update resolves floors with Math.max, so the gate cannot absorb the reduction either. The declaration's own note anticipates this and prescribes a hand edit of the number. That is the defect: in the resulting diff, repairing a witnessed defect population and silently relaxing a quality floor are byte-indistinguishable acts, both requiring the same privileged edit, so the guard cannot tell a cleanup from an erosion. Denominating the floor over informative edges (total minus redundant) makes the two motions distinguishable without any privileged act: removing an implied edge drops both terms and is neutral, while removing a load-bearing edge still breaches. Dual of pm-c90tfh, which owns the ADDITION direction (the blocks ceiling sits at 243 with zero headroom, so ordering edges cannot be added either); together the two mean the ordering relation is frozen in both directions while three open items require changing it."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["enforcement","graph","measurement-ratchet","redundancy","tracker-governance"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-10T20:46:45.822Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T20:46:45.822Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":150},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The measurement ratchet exposes a graph_analytic selector source so a declaration can be denominated over a population the graph analytics compute rather than only over the audit census; A floor exists over informative edges (total deduplicated directed edges minus the redundancy analytic's redundant_count) so that removing a witnessed implied edge is bound-neutral and removing a load-bearing edge still breaches; redundant_count carries a ceiling so the witnessed implied-ordering population can only shrink, and a run that grows it fails; The total-edge floor is retired in the same change that lands its replacement, with the re-denomination recorded in the declaration note rather than left as an unexplained lowered number; A negative control proves both directions: removing a redundant edge passes and removing an informative edge fails"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-96h7"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"graph-profile-edges-floor floor=11871 observed=11875 (headroom 4); pm graph redundancy redundant_count=73; removing 5+ redundant edges fails the release gate with floor_undercut; scripts/release/tracker-measurement-gate.mjs resolves floors with Math.max(declaration.floor, entry.observed) so --update never lowers one"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-4vz6mz","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:46:45.822Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-7ob5","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:46:45.822Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-96h7","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:46:45.822Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-c90tfh","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:46:45.822Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-g4k74y","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:46:45.822Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-w7ccmv","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:46:45.822Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"c044e38737f6e85ade1468f46b1eef833982481fc229d42fb2e0bc45f20d7fdf","message":""}
